>> B5: Briefly describe your implementation of the "wait" system call
>> and how it interacts with process termination.

The wait(pid) system call blocks the parent process until the child terminates. 
It searches for the child in child_list, ensures it hasn’t been waited on before, and 
uses sema_down(&pcb->sema_wait); to block until the child exits. When a process 
terminates (process_exit()), it signals the waiting parent with sema_up(&pcb->sema_wait)
;, allowing the parent to retrieve the child’s exit code. If 
the parent exits first, the child becomes an orphan, and its resources are only freed upon 
termination. This ensures proper synchronization and prevents resource leaks. 

